<title>SINGAPORE: Armstrong 1996 net profit up 7.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Armstrong 1996 net profit up 7.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				4.72 vs   4.40</p>
<p>    Final dividend (pct)		  5.00 vs   5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     2.66 vs   2.91</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)   2.66 vs   2.49</p>
<p>    Turnover				 42.03 vs  36.83</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.21 vs   0.21</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.14 vs   0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   1.78 vs   1.32</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  5.13 vs   5.00</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     1.60 vs   0.89</p>
<p>    Tax					 2.07 vs   1.37</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (gain) 0.05 vs   0.12 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Armstrong Industrial Corp Ltd is a precision engineering company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
